{
  "_comment": [
    "Repairs Hindi values that arrive from the upstream translation sheet as legacy-font mojibake.",
    "The sheet's Hindi column was at some point round-tripped through a non-Unicode 8-bit Devanagari",
    "font of the Kruti Dev / Chanakya / DevLys family, whose private-use slots carry the half-forms,",
    "conjuncts and matra width-variants that have no ASCII equivalent. 61 such slots survive in the",
    "published CSV, corrupting 71 of 115 ingame terms, 287 move names and 902 of 1155 Pokemon names.",
    "",
    "'kind' encodes placement, because the legacy font stores text in VISUAL order and Unicode stores",
    "it in LOGICAL order:",
    "  inline  — substitute where the marker stands",
    "  prebase — decoded matra renders LEFT of its consonant, so move it right past the whole cluster",
    "  repha   — decoded र् renders ABOVE the following consonant, so move it left in front of it",
    "",
    "Each entry carries a worked example that scripts/hi-pua-repair.mjs validateTable() re-checks on",
    "every fetch, so an edit here cannot silently change an unrelated word.",
    "",
    "Every value below was derived from context and cross-checked; none of it has been confirmed",
    "against a real Hindi Pokemon GO client. See the PR description."
  ],
  "suspectedSourceFont": "Kruti Dev / Chanakya / DevLys family (legacy 8-bit Devanagari)",
